The fix for #22 is finished and queued to land on main again, but it hasn't landed yet: build jobs are stalling across the org (looper#113). I left #22 open and set this run's outcome to `Blocked-by: tacplus-dev/looper#113`.

- **The fix:** two commits, unchanged from the last run.
  - 8cc61f2 makes both `Dockerfile` and `Dockerfile.cross` create a system user and group `oauth` with the fixed ID 65532, and end with `USER 65532:65532`. oauth writes no files, so no directory needs to be owned by that user.
  - It also adds a `dockerfile-user` step to `just gates` that fails if the Dockerfile's last `USER` isn't 65532:65532.
  - fb5ace8 bumps the version to 0.1.2 for the patch release.
- **Checked here:** semgrep (`p/default`) reports no findings on either fixed Dockerfile, though it flags `missing-user-entrypoint` on main's. `just dockerfile-user` passes. The trace check still flags only `mint_callback_tokens`, which is already #16; this change touches no handler.
- **Why it hasn't landed:** all three earlier lands ended "no verdict within 3h". The last build was marked pending at 02:23Z and never reported. No tacplus-dev service has landed code since Nov 9, and the manager took 8 to 13 hours just to start a land last time. I queued a fourth land at 05:17Z, which the manager will still run after this run ends.
- **Not verified:** that the image starts. There's no container runtime here, and no image has been built yet (#5).

I posted this status on the issue: https://github.com/tacplus-dev/oauth/issues/22#issuecomment-6788193328

Once the land succeeds, the next run checks that `just gates` passes on main, tags and pushes `v0.1.2`, comments and closes the issue. If the land times out again, that run re-lands it after looper#113 is closed.
